# Multi-device database schema

Source of truth UI: canvas `multi-device-db-schema.canvas.tsx`  
Related behavior: `.cursor/rules/vpn-sessions-live-only.mdc`

Do **not** put `vpn_ip` / `device_id` / `vpn_public_key` back on `access_keys`.  
Do **not** put `vpn_ip` on `devices`.  
Do **not** add soft-close fields to `vpn_sessions` (`active`, `ended_at`, history).

## Tables

```text
access_keys
  id
  key
  status          # created | activated | revoked

devices           # bind only; 1 key → N devices
  id
  access_key_id   # FK → access_keys.id
  device_id       # client vault id
  platform        # windows | android | …
  vpn_public_key

vpn_sessions      # live online slots only
  id
  access_key_id   # FK → access_keys.id
  device_id       # FK → devices.id (PK устройства, не client string)
  vpn_ip
  started_at      # set on connect (now); gone when row DELETE’d
```

Relations: `access_keys` 1→N `devices`; device 0..1 live `vpn_sessions` row.

## Lifecycle

| Action | DB |
|---|---|
| create key | INSERT `access_keys` (`created`) |
| bind | INSERT `devices`; key → `activated` if first device |
| connect | if `COUNT(vpn_sessions for key) < MAX_ACTIVE_SESSIONS` → INSERT session + `vpn_ip` + `started_at` + peer |
| disconnect / revoke cleanup | DELETE `vpn_sessions` row(s) + remove peer(s) |
| unbind | DELETE device (cascades session if any) |

Limit: **2 устройства одновременно в VPN** (`MAX_ACTIVE_SESSIONS = 2` in
`backend/app/core/limits.py`). Count **live `vpn_sessions`**, not rows in `devices`
(привязок может быть больше 2). Raise to 3 later (Excel #53).

`started_at`: wall-clock start of the live slot (UI timer / diagnostics). Not session history.

## Out of scope until asked

- remote disconnect
- closed-session history
- sticky `vpn_ip` across reconnects (optional later)
- `expires_at` / paid subscription columns on keys
